     new: Yes. Given a mechanism x and an equilibrium s, the direct mechanism x_hat(theta) = x(s(theta)) makes truthful reporting an equilibrium, and each type receives the same outcome as under x and s (Proposition 2.2). Assumption 3 is one agent with finite type, message and outcome sets. Nothing is proved for several agents.
